Experimental hi-hat sounds made by resampling some of the samples recorded for the Red and Green banks through my late grandfather's Marantz tape recorder, a machine that plays too slow and wobbles like crazy. Recorded onto one of my mom's old tapes, dubbed over country recordings who-knows-how-many times. Intentionally, extremely lo-fi.  This one has a ton of character and benefits from playing with the pitch knob to find sweet spots of dark, haunting hats. Filter to taste.}